==Serbo-Croatian==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|sh|sla-pro|*kako}}.

===Pronunciation===
* (kȁko) {{IPA|sh|/kâko/}}
* (kàko) {{IPA|sh|/kǎko/}}

===Adverb===
{{sh-adverb|head=kȁko}} ''or'' {{sh-adverb|head=kàko}}

# [[how]] (in what way)
# [[so]] (used as a modifier to indicate surprise, delight, or other strong feelings)
#: {{ux|sh|'''Kako''' je dobro!|It's so good!|inline=1}}

===Conjunction===
{{sh-conjunction}}

# [[as]], [[while]] (links or emphasizes two or more events which happen and vary through time, in order or simultaneously)
#: {{ux|sh|'''Kako''' je noć odmicala, sve sam više bio uspavaniji.|As the night went on, I was getting increasingly sleepier.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|sh|Croatia|used with [[present conditional]]}} [[to]], [[so]], [[so as to]], [[so that]], [[in order to]], [[in order for]] (expresses a past or future intent that refers to the present)
#: {{ux|sh|Preselio se ovdje '''kako''' bi našao posao.|t=He moved here to find work.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|sh|'''Kako''' bi se jednog dana i mi mogli natjecati, moramo puno vježbati.|t=In order for us to compete one day, we need to train a lot.|inline=1}}

===Related terms===
* {{l|sh|kao}}

